<title>INDIA: India's Grasim 96/97 1st half net lower.</title>
<headline>India's Grasim 96/97 1st half net lower.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   1,474.4  vs   1,688.5</p>
<p>    Net sales	   14,830.2  vs  13,290.0</p>
<p>    Other income	   723.2  vs   1,134.7</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 11,841.8  vs  10,584.4</p>
<p>    Interest	     1,291.9  vs   1,133.6</p>
<p>    Gross profit	 2,419.7  vs   2,706.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   652.8  vs     598.2</p>
<p>    Tax			292.5  vs     420.0</p>
<p>Note: Grasim Industries, a diversified firm is part of the Aditya Birla group of companies. The firm said the abnormal delay in the arrival of monsoons at Nagda affected Viscose Staple Fibre (VSF) output for 46 days during June and July 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
